        "date": "2026-11-25T11:21:56Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(multiaxis): Rotary Flow field-eye parity and the radial link C unwind\n\nAdmit OpParams::RotaryFlow on the field eye: rotary_kind_lift answers\nOk(()) on a measured parity - the laid bar's neck band, 168 sphere-cut\ntops within 1.27e-5 of the swept-ball law (bound 2.01e-5), 0 sign\nmisses over 7,053 cell centres, 35,491 sub-chords at the verdict\nclass, the eye 2,131 sub-chords in 3.0 s - recorded in\ndocs/decisions/2828-rotaryflow-parity.md. The column verdict still\nrefuses the kind by name; only the eye cuts it.\n\nWire the C unwind for the kind's own link shape: the gate's boolean\nbecomes Unwind { NoProof, Axial, Radial }, and Rotary Flow - whose\nband links rest on the retract cylinder, never over an axial plane -\nunwinds by whole turns at its radial retract links. The cl law reads\na feed retract's end as the arrival at rest (the mirror of the\nplunge-start rule it already kept), so the flow kernel's cut-feed\nexit off a pass no longer poisons the cylinder it rests on; every\ninserted orbit is still judged by the verifier, the solid bar and\nthe post gate. Rotary Contour keeps the axial plane; Parallel and\nOffset are refused where they would rewind, by name, the words now\nnaming both proven kinds.\n\nThe multi-pass band on the shipped millturn (C -360..360, stated\nrates) unwinds at its retract links and stays inside the travel; a\nstated travel with no C rate refuses the rewind by name (#906), and\na pass wider than the travel refuses with no clear link to unwind\nat.\n\nFixes #2828",
